        {
          "path": "_m/e/y/5/1/hassan-tower-wp/hassan-tower-mausoleum-of-moha-1.jpg",
          "filename": "Hassan Tower - Mausoleum of Mohammed V (5508513891).jpg",
          "caption": "The Mausoleum of Mohammed V is a historical building located on the opposite side of the Hassan Tower on the Yacoub al-Mansour esplanade in Rabat, Morocco. It contains the tombs of the Moroccan king and his two sons, late King Hassan II and Prince Abdallah. The building is considered a masterpiece of modern Alaouite dynasty architecture, with its white silhouette, topped by a typical green tiled roof. Its construction was completed in 1971. Hassan II was buried there following his death in 1999 [Wikipedia.org]",
